  "description": "This course covers fundamental and advanced concepts in Pattern Recognition, including supervised and unsupervised learning algorithms such as Gaussian Mixture Models, K-means clustering, and Support Vector Machines; feature extraction techniques like Principal Component Analysis and Linear Discriminant Analysis; deep learning approaches using Convolutional Neural Networks and Autoencoders; pattern classification frameworks such as the Bayes classifier and Hidden Markov Models; and evaluation metrics like precision, recall, and F1-score. It also explores standard datasets like MNIST and CIFAR-10, and industry tools such as TensorFlow and PyTorch for implementing pattern recognition systems.",
